# `owned <name>` has to name a function the compiler can actually call, and
# until 2026-09-07 three ways of getting that wrong were `internal error` at
# exit 2 — the compiler blaming itself for a typo in a `.hero` file, which is
# the one shape CLAUDE.md §7 forbids (§4.19; panel 109's condition 1).
#
# WHY THE PROBE COULD NOT CATCH THESE. Step 4a made the probe type a freer's
# parameter `char *`, so a freer whose header refutes it is `ffi_freer_type`.
# A probe is emitted per `extern`, so **a name no `extern` declares has no
# probe at all** — and a two-parameter freer's probe compiles perfectly well,
# because the probe calls it with two arguments while the release calls it
# with one. Both fell through to the lowering, which found no freer, fell back
# to a plain call, and left clang refusing `assigning to 'h_0opt_…' from
# incompatible type 'const char *'`.
#
# THE THREE SHAPES, each measured at exit 2 before the repair:
#   1. a name nothing declares — a typo;
#   2. a HEROES function of this program, which is the plausible mistake: the
#      word `owned` reads as *this frees it*, and a reader reaches for the
#      function they can see. It gets its own note, because the answer is not
#      *rename it* but *a freer is C's*;
#   3. an `extern` of the right name and the wrong arity, which its own header
#      declares honestly — nothing about it is a typo, and only the release's
#      one argument makes it wrong.
#
# This is a `check` case on purpose: `heroes check` never runs clang, so the
# refusal is proved to rest on the DECLARATIONS alone and not on a header
# being present. That is what makes it reachable in a bindings module nobody
# has compiled yet.
extern "string.h"
    function strdup(s: cstr) -> cstr owned bogus_name  #~ unknown_freer
    function strndup(s: cstr, n: u64) -> cstr owned my_own_free  #~ unknown_freer

extern "stdio.h"
    function fopen(path: cstr, mode: cstr) -> ptr
    function fwrite(p: ptr, size: u64, n: u64, f: ptr) -> u64
    # The arity refusal, on a name this group really does declare.
    function tmpnam(buffer: ptr) -> cstr owned fwrite  #~ freer_arity

# The Heroes function shape 2 reaches for. It is a real function of this
# program, which is exactly why naming it as a freer has to be refused rather
# than quietly accepted.
function my_own_free(p: ptr)
    _ = p

function main()
    print(0)
